WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.710
When Orchard Core runs on several servers, each one keeps its own cache,

00:00:05.710 --> 00:00:08.186
locks, signals and encryption keys.

00:00:08.186 --> 00:00:11.387
The Redis module moves them to a shared server.

00:00:11.387 --> 00:00:16.460
In this video, we'll connect a site to Redis and see what each feature shares.

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:24.417
By default, each server keeps its state to itself.

00:00:24.417 --> 00:00:28.614
Its cache is in its own memory, its signals and locks reach only

00:00:28.614 --> 00:00:33.110
its own code, and its data protection keys are files on its own disk.

00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:36.562
The Redis module replaces these defaults.

00:00:36.562 --> 00:00:41.333
One feature holds the connection, and four more share the cache, the signals,

00:00:41.333 --> 00:00:43.920
the locks and the keys between servers.

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:50.981
Start a Redis server, for example in Docker.

00:00:50.981 --> 00:00:56.073
The Redis feature reads its connection from the Redis section of the configuration.

00:00:56.073 --> 00:01:00.650
Configuration is the connection string, and it is the only required value.

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:06.536
InstancePrefix starts every key, so applications can share one Redis server.

00:01:06.536 --> 00:01:12.863
AllowAdmin permits admin commands, which the data protection feature uses to check persistence.

00:01:12.863 --> 00:01:17.310
DisableCertificateVerification accepts a self-signed certificate.

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:23.086
Tenants with the same connection string share one connection, and each tenant prefixes

00:01:23.086 --> 00:01:26.200
its keys with the instance prefix and its own name.

00:01:26.950 --> 00:01:30.981
If Configuration is missing or invalid, the module logs an error.

00:01:30.981 --> 00:01:35.807
The tenant keeps running on its defaults, the Redis features stay inactive, and

00:01:35.807 --> 00:01:38.930
the health check reports the server as unhealthy.

00:01:43.138 --> 00:01:45.986
Features are managed in Tools, Features.

00:01:45.986 --> 00:01:51.621
Search for OrchardCore.Redis, the start of the feature IDs, and five features appear.

00:01:51.621 --> 00:01:57.008
Four are in the Distributed category, and the data protection one is in Security.

00:01:57.458 --> 00:02:01.576
Redis Cache depends on Redis, so enabling it enables both.

00:02:01.576 --> 00:02:03.828
Select Enable on Redis Cache.

00:02:03.828 --> 00:02:08.718
The page reloads, and a message confirms that Redis Cache was enabled.

00:02:09.186 --> 00:02:12.811
Search again, and Redis and Redis Cache are both enabled.

00:02:12.811 --> 00:02:17.932
To enable several features at once, select them, and choose Enable in Bulk Actions.

00:02:17.932 --> 00:02:20.636
Let's do it for Redis Bus and Redis Lock.

00:02:21.091 --> 00:02:25.080
Redis, Redis Cache, Redis Bus and Redis Lock are enabled.

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:28.689
Distributed Data Protection (Redis) stays disabled:

00:02:28.689 --> 00:02:33.501
it is recommended only with a Redis server configured for persistence.

00:02:37.699 --> 00:02:40.794
To check the connection, enable Health Checks.

00:02:40.794 --> 00:02:45.317
When Health Checks and Redis are both enabled, the Redis module adds a

00:02:45.317 --> 00:02:47.519
check named Redis Health Check.

00:02:47.977 --> 00:02:50.043
The endpoint is /health/live.

00:02:50.043 --> 00:02:56.360
With ShowDetails on in the Health Checks section of the configuration, the response lists each check.

00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:58.485
Redis Health Check is Healthy:

00:02:58.485 --> 00:03:02.617
the site connected to the server and received a reply to a ping.

00:03:03.078 --> 00:03:10.707
With ShowDetails off, the endpoint returns only the status, and Unhealthy returns 503 Service Unavailable.

00:03:10.707 --> 00:03:15.816
It needs no sign-in, so turn ShowDetails on only when the endpoint is

00:03:15.816 --> 00:03:19.018
restricted to trusted monitoring clients.

00:03:23.218 --> 00:03:27.984
Redis Cache replaces the in-memory distributed cache of the tenant with Redis.

00:03:27.984 --> 00:03:32.637
Orchard Core keeps documents there, such as the site settings and the roles,

00:03:32.637 --> 00:03:36.438
and the Dynamic Cache module keeps its rendered output there.

00:03:37.188 --> 00:03:39.417
It also replaces the tag cache.

00:03:39.417 --> 00:03:43.875
Cached items are grouped under tags, and the tags are kept in Redis,

00:03:43.875 --> 00:03:47.128
so every server sees the same items under a tag.

00:03:51.328 --> 00:03:55.951
Orchard Core raises signals to tell caches to refresh, and by default they

00:03:55.951 --> 00:03:58.552
reach only the server that raised them.

00:03:58.552 --> 00:04:03.349
Redis Bus registers a message bus, and the signal service then publishes each

00:04:03.349 --> 00:04:05.198
signal to a Redis channel.

00:04:05.948 --> 00:04:11.604
Every server subscribes to that channel, and signals its own caches when a message arrives.

00:04:11.604 --> 00:04:15.861
Each message carries the host name and process ID of its sender, so

00:04:15.861 --> 00:04:18.718
a server ignores the messages it published.

00:04:22.918 --> 00:04:28.047
By default, the distributed lock is local, and holds back only its own server.

00:04:28.047 --> 00:04:32.138
Redis Lock takes it in Redis instead, so one server at a time

00:04:32.138 --> 00:04:36.168
holds a name, until it releases it or its expiration passes.

00:04:36.918 --> 00:04:42.810
Auto Setup takes this lock, so servers that share a database set a site up once.

00:04:42.810 --> 00:04:46.988
Add Redis Lock to the setup features beside Auto Setup.

00:04:46.988 --> 00:04:54.798
LockTimeout and LockExpiration are in milliseconds; set both or neither, and each defaults to sixty seconds.

00:04:55.548 --> 00:04:57.515
Background tasks use it too.

00:04:57.515 --> 00:05:01.448
A task that sets a LockTimeout and a LockExpiration is atomic:

00:05:01.448 --> 00:05:05.033
it still runs on every server, but never on two at once.

00:05:05.033 --> 00:05:08.388
Without a distributed lock, both values are ignored.

00:05:12.588 --> 00:05:20.258
Data protection encrypts authentication cookies, anti-forgery tokens and stored secrets, such as an SMTP password.

00:05:20.258 --> 00:05:24.668
Every server of a site needs the same keys, and by default each

00:05:24.668 --> 00:05:27.928
server keeps them in its own App_Data folder.

00:05:28.678 --> 00:05:37.352
Distributed Data Protection (Redis) stores the keys under the instance prefix, the tenant name and DataProtection-Keys.

00:05:37.352 --> 00:05:39.780
This key ring is not a cache.

00:05:39.780 --> 00:05:44.568
Give Redis persistence, with AOF or RDB, and a backup strategy.

00:05:45.318 --> 00:05:49.135
The module logs a warning unless it can confirm that persistence is on,

00:05:49.135 --> 00:05:53.001
which it can only do when admin commands are allowed, with AllowAdmin or

00:05:53.001 --> 00:05:54.538
in the connection string.

00:05:58.738 --> 00:06:01.693
Your own modules can use the same connection.

00:06:01.693 --> 00:06:04.126
Take IRedisService in a constructor:

00:06:04.126 --> 00:06:07.660
it is registered whenever the Redis feature is enabled.

00:06:07.660 --> 00:06:12.758
When the configuration is invalid, it is a NullRedisService, which never connects.

00:06:13.508 --> 00:06:17.601
Connection and Database are null until a connection is created.

00:06:17.601 --> 00:06:23.118
Check Database, call ConnectAsync if needed, and handle a failure, because a connection

00:06:23.118 --> 00:06:25.728
does not mean the server is reachable.

00:06:26.478 --> 00:06:30.559
A feature that replaces a default service with one that relies on Redis

00:06:30.559 --> 00:06:33.740
should do it only when IsRedisConfigured returns true.

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:36.178
Otherwise, the tenant keeps the default.

00:06:38.178 --> 00:06:39.778
That's the Redis module:

00:06:39.778 --> 00:06:43.725
one shared server for the cache, the signals, the locks and the data

00:06:43.725 --> 00:06:46.391
protection keys of every instance of a site.

00:06:46.391 --> 00:06:47.778
Thanks for watching.

